SUMMARY:Worcester 20s & 30s 2nd Annual Hostel Takeover Weekend in the Whit
 e Mountains
LOCATION:36 Washington Street\nConway\, NH 03818
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, June 26\, 2026 | 8:00 PM\nhttps://activities.outdoors
 .org/s/oc-activity/a5UVX00000152yH2AQ/\nJoin the Worcester Chapter 20s & 3
 0s for a weekend of outdoor fun in the White Mountains June 26-29 for the 
 second annual Hostel Takeover! This year’s theme is…aliens! Expect the
  theme to crop up throughout the trip\; participation in it is optional!Th
 e trip runs from the evening of Friday\, June 26 through Monday\, June 29.
  A variety of hiking and socializing opportunities will be offered each da
 y as we explore several regions of the White Mountains. At least two hikin
 g options\, one moderate and one vigorous\, will be provided each day (for
  rating definitions\, go here). Specific offerings will be determined by l
 eaders that weekend depending on participant ability and conditions. Hikes
  will be in the immediate area and possibly others farther afield. After 
 the days’ hikes\, we will all return to the Conway Hostel (CoHo)\, our b
 asecamp for the weekend. The trip includes three nights’ lodging at CoHo
 \, where you will find all the comforts you are looking for after a long h
 ike– shared bunk rooms\, private bathrooms\, a shared kitchen with full 
 access\, and shared space for socializing. A group dinner will be included
  and served on Saturday and Sunday evening\, and CoHo offers free coffee\,
  tea\, and granola bars for breakfasts. Friday night dinner will be an opt
 ional potluck. Breakfast (other than what the hostel offers) and lunches n
 ot included. Evening activities will be offered\, possibilities including
  a movie screening\, star gazing\, fire pit\, and games. The hostel is als
 o a ~5 minute walk away from the Saco River where swimming is allowed.Cost
  is $170 for AMC members ($185 for non-members) per person for 3 nights at
  CoHo and 2 dinners. If the cost of this trip is an obstacle for you being
  able to attend\, please reach out to one of the registration leaders (Ale
 xandra at amusic@verizon.net or Dirk at dirkauman@gmail.com)\, as we have 
 limited subsidy options available. Refunds are not guaranteed and are depe
 ndent on someone taking your spot if this event reaches full capacity. On
 ce you register for the trip here\, one of the leaders will send a screeni
 ng form to gather further information to ensure the trip will be safe and 
 fun for all participants. Payment will be collected once your spot on the 
 trip has been confirmed.Gear is available for loan through the Worcester C
 hapter Gear Shed for those who may need it. As an affinity group within A
 MC that is dedicated to encouraging people in their 20s and 30s to enjoy t
 he outdoors\, this is a trip for those in their 20s and 30s.
END:VEVENT
